@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm start` to serve the site (default port: 11222).
+
+## Local service connections
+
+Serve the deployed page over HTTPS. Localhost is a secure-context exception for
+development. In **Connect a local service**, choose a local network device or a
+loopback service, enter its full HTTP/HTTPS resource URL, and select **Connect**.
+The page sends a GET request only after this action and displays the response as
+plain text. No device discovery or automatic connection runs on page load.
+
+The browser controls access through its network permissions. If access is blocked,
+allow Local network or Loopback network access in the browser's site settings.
+Browsers without the permission-query API still attempt the connection on click;
+their normal network and mixed-content restrictions apply.
+
+The device or companion service must be running and return standard CORS headers
+allowing the page's origin, for example `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://your-site.example`.
+This app does not bypass CORS or browser permissions. Production hosting must not
+disable `local-network` or `loopback-network` in its Permissions-Policy. If the
+page is embedded across origins, the parent must delegate both permissions via
+the iframe's `allow` attribute and its Permissions-Policy configuration.
